From 715a60bd4539c6e4ffbb2627675c44219ade7431 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jose Fernandez <me@jrfernandez.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:11:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] dxil: Guard signed integer division by zero.

Comment (Hans-Kristian): It has not been confirmed yet that this
analysis is real. sdiv/srem behavior has been confirmed against native D3D12 drivers
however.

The Witcher 3 with ray tracing halts the GPU on NVIDIA a few
seconds into every world load. On vkd3d-proton 3.0.1 every crash
dump taken at the hang (Nsight Aftermath, RTX 5090, 610.57.04)
shows the same thing, every running thread group inside one loop of
one compute shader and none at the division just before it.
Simplified, the shader is:

  stride = m / n;                         /* line 205, n is 0 here */
  for (i = 0; i != n; i++)                /* should run zero times */
      list[base + i] = (i * stride) % m;  /* lines 221 to 225 */

Where the thread groups were. The other dumps look the same:

  warps  PC            SPIR-V
     23  0x8a0..0xa90  221  %155 = OpSRem %uint %154 %152
      1  0xa70         222  %156 = OpIAdd %uint %147 %138
      7  0x870..0xb20  225  OpStore %157 %158 Aligned 8
      0                205  %136 = OpSDiv %uint %130 %124

n is a signed per-probe ray count. Reducing the shader to a few
lines and varying one thing at a time showed why the loop runs:
once the compiler has seen x / n it behaves as if n != 0, so the
loop loses its entry check, and with n really zero it runs until i
wraps around. Adding an explicit if (n != 0) around the loop does
not help, the compiler removes that check the same way.

build_udiv_umod already guards udiv and urem against exactly this.
But sdiv and srem are still emitted bare. Move them to
emit_integer_division_instruction, where udiv and urem already get
the helper. It branches on a zero divisor and returns -1, so the
division is never reached with a zero and the compiler cannot
conclude anything about n. Sign extension of narrow operands was
added there as needed. With this change the game no longer hangs.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
